# Remote timeouts and retries

This repo currently does **no** remote/network I/O — the TSP optimizer runs
entirely offline. This rule is a **forward guardrail**: the first time any code
here talks to a network peer (an HTTP API, a `fetch()` from a future UI, a
webhook, a package index, a `gh`/`curl` helper), it must follow the constraints
below. Org template sync: repository-helpers#570.

## Timeouts (required)

- Set an **explicit timeout** on every remote call (connect + read, or a single
  overall deadline the library supports). `fetch()` has no default timeout — pass
  an `AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`. Node `http`/`https`, `undici`, and any SDK client
  get a finite, documented timeout from a shared config value — never library
  defaults that mean "wait forever".
- Agent / shell wrappers that hit the network should use the helpers'
  `--timeout` / `run_command … --timeout` patterns when available.

## Retries (required when retrying)

- **Retryable set:** network errors / timeout / connection reset, and HTTP
  `408`, `429`, `502`, `503`, `504`. Everything else — including `400`, `401`,
  `403`, `404`, `500`, `501` — is permanent; surface it, don't retry.
- Cap attempts (small fixed `N`, 2–5) **or** a total retry budget. Back off
  between attempts (exponential with jitter). Honor `Retry-After` when the peer
  sends it, clamped to a ceiling with a wall-clock deadline.
- Do **not** retry a non-idempotent write (`POST`/`PUT`/`PATCH`/`DELETE`) unless
  the API contract is safe (dedupe keys / explicit idempotency). Idempotent reads
  are safe to retry within budget. Prefer fail fast on 4xx except `408` / `429`.
- Log or surface a clear timeout / retry-exhaustion error (non-zero CLI exit /
  visible error) — never spin silently.

## Anti-patterns

```ts
// bad — no timeout
const res = await fetch(url);

// bad — unbounded retry
while (true) {
  try { return await fetch(url); }
  catch { /* forever */ }
}
```

```ts
// good — explicit timeout + bounded, backed-off retry of an idempotent read
const RETRYABLE = new Set([408, 429, 502, 503, 504]);
for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxAttempts; attempt++) {
  try {
    const res = await fetch(url, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(timeoutMs) });
    if (res.ok || !RETRYABLE.has(res.status)) return res; // permanent -> stop
  } catch (e) {
    const retryable =
      e instanceof TypeError || // network failure ("fetch failed")
      (e instanceof DOMException &&
        (e.name === 'TimeoutError' || e.name === 'AbortError')); // AbortSignal.timeout() / manual abort
    if (!retryable) throw e;
  }
  if (attempt === maxAttempts) throw new Error('request timed out / retries exhausted');
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, backoffMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1)));
}
```
